comments.body:
@participant8 I am the author of several issue of pointing to more emphasis towards customization (like the #7274 you linked), and parameterizing the theme options would already be a big steps in the right direction without having to rely on CSS all the time - +1 for this approach

> `font: "sans serif" | "serif" | "monospace" | str (custom font URL)`

It would be very useful to also allow pointing to a local static font. Some enterprise network have security controls that can break such dependencies in my experience.
